<!--
  One deck's page on the GRID tab of the Overview panel (effects.xml): the
  beat grid editor. The panel sits directly beside the waveforms, so the beat
  markers you are correcting stay on screen while you correct them.

  Began as the side-panel grid controls in PiFlex
  <https://github.com/xsploit/PiFlex> by Tyler "subsect", and was reworked
  here; see LICENSE.

  The deck tabs at the top are part of the page, not of the tab bar above it,
  so both pages carry an identical pair and the bar looks continuous while the
  stack swaps under it. A tab writes its deck's stack trigger, which both
  selects the deck and lights the tab: WWidgetStack holds the visible page's
  trigger at 1 and the rest at 0, so the same connection drives the press and
  the highlight. Select-only, like the FX / KEY tabs and the cue drawer — a
  tap on the deck already showing is a no-op.

  Every action is a stock BpmControl push control on [Channel<N>] and edits
  the loaded track's grid in place (Mixxx writes it back to the library):

    Earlier / Later    beats_translate_{earlier,later}  - 10 ms per step
    Align              beats_translate_curpos           - nearest beat to playhead
    BPM - / +          beats_adjust_{slower,faster}     - 0.01 BPM per step
    /2 and x2          beats_set_{halve,double}         - fix a doubled analysis
    Undo               beats_undo_adjustment            - one step back

  The two step sizes are deliberately fine, which makes them useless as single
  taps: nudging a grid 200 ms would be twenty presses. Those four buttons are
  <Repeat>ing, so holding one keeps it firing, and the repeat accelerates — a
  brief hold still steps finely, a long one covers ground (see
  WPushButton::slotRepeat).

  Align sits at the end of the row, away from the two arrows: it snaps the grid
  to the playhead, so it throws away the nudging the arrows beside it just did.
  "Align" rather than "Reset" because Undo, two rows down, is the button that
  restores the analyzed grid — two reverts named alike would be worse.

  Undo takes its enabled state from beats_undo_possible. Greyed out it swallows
  the tap outright — a disabled WWidget never synthesizes touch -> mouse — so
  there is no way to "undo" past the loaded grid. The action block as a whole
  follows track_loaded for the same reason: no track, no grid to edit.

  Variables:
    channel: channel number (e.g. 1, 2)
-->
<Template>
  <WidgetGroup>
    <ObjectName>Grid_DeckPage_<Variable name="channel"/></ObjectName>
    <Layout>vertical</Layout>
    <SizePolicy>me,me</SizePolicy>
    <Children>

      <WidgetGroup>
        <ObjectName>Grid_DeckBar</ObjectName>
        <Layout>horizontal</Layout>
        <Size>0me,30f</Size>
        <Children>
          <PushButton>
            <ObjectName>Grid_DeckTab1</ObjectName>
            <Size>32f,30f</Size>
            <NumberStates>2</NumberStates>
            <State>
              <Number>0</Number>
              <Text>1</Text>
            </State>
            <State>
              <Number>1</Number>
              <Text>1</Text>
            </State>
            <LeftClickIsPushButton>true</LeftClickIsPushButton>
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Skin],grid_deck1</ConfigKey>
              <EmitOnDownPress>true</EmitOnDownPress>
            </Connection>
          </PushButton>
          <PushButton>
            <ObjectName>Grid_DeckTab2</ObjectName>
            <Size>32f,30f</Size>
            <NumberStates>2</NumberStates>
            <State>
              <Number>0</Number>
              <Text>2</Text>
            </State>
            <State>
              <Number>1</Number>
              <Text>2</Text>
            </State>
            <LeftClickIsPushButton>true</LeftClickIsPushButton>
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Skin],grid_deck2</ConfigKey>
              <EmitOnDownPress>true</EmitOnDownPress>
            </Connection>
          </PushButton>

          <!-- The grid's own BPM, not the deck's: local_bpm ignores the rate
               slider, so the number only moves when the grid itself does. -->
          <NumberBpm>
            <ObjectName>Grid_Bpm</ObjectName>
            <Size>0me,30f</Size>
            <NumberOfDigits>2</NumberOfDigits>
            <Alignment>right</Alignment>
            <Channel><Variable name="channel"/></Channel>
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],local_bpm</ConfigKey>
            </Connection>
          </NumberBpm>
        </Children>
      </WidgetGroup>

      <WidgetGroup>
        <ObjectName>Grid_Actions</ObjectName>
        <Layout>vertical</Layout>
        <SizePolicy>me,me</SizePolicy>
        <Children>

          <WidgetGroup>
            <ObjectName>Grid_ButtonRow</ObjectName>
            <Layout>horizontal</Layout>
            <Size>0me,42f</Size>
            <Children>
              <PushButton>
                <ObjectName>Grid_Nudge</ObjectName>
                <Size>0me,42f</Size>
                <NumberStates>1</NumberStates>
                <State>
                  <Number>0</Number>
                  <Text>&#9664;</Text>
                </State>
                <Repeat>true</Repeat>
                <Connection>
                  <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],beats_translate_earlier</ConfigKey>
                  <ConnectValueToWidget>false</ConnectValueToWidget>
                </Connection>
              </PushButton>
              <PushButton>
                <ObjectName>Grid_Nudge</ObjectName>
                <Size>0me,42f</Size>
                <NumberStates>1</NumberStates>
                <State>
                  <Number>0</Number>
                  <Text>&#9654;</Text>
                </State>
                <Repeat>true</Repeat>
                <Connection>
                  <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],beats_translate_later</ConfigKey>
                  <ConnectValueToWidget>false</ConnectValueToWidget>
                </Connection>
              </PushButton>
              <PushButton>
                <ObjectName>Grid_Align</ObjectName>
                <Size>0me,42f</Size>
                <NumberStates>1</NumberStates>
                <State>
                  <Number>0</Number>
                  <Text>Align</Text>
                </State>
                <Connection>
                  <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],beats_translate_curpos</ConfigKey>
                  <ConnectValueToWidget>false</ConnectValueToWidget>
                  <EmitOnDownPress>true</EmitOnDownPress>
                </Connection>
              </PushButton>
            </Children>
          </WidgetGroup>

          <WidgetGroup>
            <ObjectName>Grid_ButtonRow</ObjectName>
            <Layout>horizontal</Layout>
            <Size>0me,42f</Size>
            <Children>
              <PushButton>
                <ObjectName>Grid_Bpm_Down</ObjectName>
                <Size>0me,42f</Size>
                <NumberStates>1</NumberStates>
                <State>
                  <Number>0</Number>
                  <Text>BPM &#8722;</Text>
                </State>
                <Repeat>true</Repeat>
                <Connection>
                  <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],beats_adjust_slower</ConfigKey>
                  <ConnectValueToWidget>false</ConnectValueToWidget>
                </Connection>
              </PushButton>
              <PushButton>
                <ObjectName>Grid_Bpm_Up</ObjectName>
                <Size>0me,42f</Size>
                <NumberStates>1</NumberStates>
                <State>
                  <Number>0</Number>
                  <Text>BPM +</Text>
                </State>
                <Repeat>true</Repeat>
                <Connection>
                  <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],beats_adjust_faster</ConfigKey>
                  <ConnectValueToWidget>false</ConnectValueToWidget>
                </Connection>
              </PushButton>
            </Children>
          </WidgetGroup>

          <WidgetGroup>
            <ObjectName>Grid_ButtonRow</ObjectName>
            <Layout>horizontal</Layout>
            <Size>0me,44f</Size>
            <Children>
              <PushButton>
                <ObjectName>Grid_Scale</ObjectName>
                <Size>0me,44f</Size>
                <NumberStates>1</NumberStates>
                <State>
                  <Number>0</Number>
                  <Text>&#247;2</Text>
                </State>
                <Connection>
                  <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],beats_set_halve</ConfigKey>
                  <ConnectValueToWidget>false</ConnectValueToWidget>
                  <EmitOnDownPress>true</EmitOnDownPress>
                </Connection>
              </PushButton>
              <PushButton>
                <ObjectName>Grid_Scale</ObjectName>
                <Size>0me,44f</Size>
                <NumberStates>1</NumberStates>
                <State>
                  <Number>0</Number>
                  <Text>&#215;2</Text>
                </State>
                <Connection>
                  <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],beats_set_double</ConfigKey>
                  <ConnectValueToWidget>false</ConnectValueToWidget>
                  <EmitOnDownPress>true</EmitOnDownPress>
                </Connection>
              </PushButton>
              <PushButton>
                <ObjectName>Grid_Undo</ObjectName>
                <Size>0me,44f</Size>
                <NumberStates>1</NumberStates>
                <State>
                  <Number>0</Number>
                  <Text>Undo</Text>
                </State>
                <Connection>
                  <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],beats_undo_adjustment</ConfigKey>
                  <ConnectValueToWidget>false</ConnectValueToWidget>
                  <EmitOnDownPress>true</EmitOnDownPress>
                </Connection>
                <Connection>
                  <ConnectValueFromWidget>false</ConnectValueFromWidget>
                  <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],beats_undo_possible</ConfigKey>
                  <BindProperty>enabled</BindProperty>
                </Connection>
              </PushButton>
            </Children>
          </WidgetGroup>

        </Children>
        <Connection>
          <ConnectValueFromWidget>false</ConnectValueFromWidget>
          <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],track_loaded</ConfigKey>
          <BindProperty>enabled</BindProperty>
        </Connection>
      </WidgetGroup>

    </Children>
  </WidgetGroup>
</Template>
